## Improving these instructions

- Watch for gaps that no instruction file or skill covers: a correction I give twice, a command or procedure you rebuilt by hand, a workaround for a tool failure, or a decision I made the same way twice.
- Log each gap in `~/.agents/improvements.md` before you tell me about it. Read the log first, and add a sighting to a matching entry rather than starting a new one. The log's top says where a fix belongs and how to write the entry.
- Edit an instruction file or skill only after I approve the entry.
- chezmoi generates `~/.agents/AGENTS.md`, so never edit it directly. Edit `home/dot_agents/AGENTS.md.tmpl` in `{{ .chezmoi.workingTree }}`, or `~/.agents/AGENTS.work.md` for a machine's own section, then run `chezmoi apply`.

## Maintaining this file

Keep this file for knowledge useful to almost every agent session, in any project.
Point to the authoritative file or command instead of repeating what it shows.
Prefer rewriting or pruning existing entries over appending new ones.
When updating this file, keep this bar and keep entries concise.
